Let a pause keep a paused RTSP session alive.

An RTSP server ends a session it has not heard from within the timeout it announced, usually 60
seconds, and a paused session is no exception. The demuxer sends its keepalive, GET_PARAMETER or
OPTIONS, only from rtsp_read_packet after a packet arrived, and a paused client reads nothing, so a
pause longer than the timeout lost the session and the play after it was refused. av_read_pause on
a stream that was not playing returned at once.

av_read_pause on a stream that is not playing now sends the same keepalive the read sends, by the
same rule: GET_PARAMETER when the server offers it and OPTIONS otherwise, once half the session
timeout has passed since the last request or the authentication went stale. It waits for the
reply, because nobody reads the connection while paused, and a refusal is returned as the error of
the pause. A caller keeps a paused session by pausing again every second or so. A stream that is
playing pauses exactly as before, and the demuxer's own internal pauses are unchanged, so nothing
changes for a caller that never pauses twice.

Applied by BuildFFmpegTask before configure.

diff --git a/libavformat/rtspdec.c b/libavformat/rtspdec.c
index 4f970d4..ee47a30 100644
--- a/libavformat/rtspdec.c
+++ b/libavformat/rtspdec.c
@@ -594,6 +594,37 @@ static int rtsp_read_play(AVFormatContext *s)
     return 0;
 }
 
+/* A client that is not playing reads nothing, so the keepalive in
+ * rtsp_read_packet never runs, and the server ends the session once its
+ * timeout passes. A pause while not playing sends that keepalive when it is
+ * due, and waits for the reply, so nothing is left unread on the connection
+ * while nobody reads it. */
+static int rtsp_keep_session_alive(AVFormatContext *s)
+{
+    RTSPState *rt = s->priv_data;
+    RTSPMessageHeader reply1, *reply = &reply1;
+    const char *method;
+    int ret;
+
+    if ((rt->rtsp_flags & RTSP_FLAG_LISTEN) || !rt->session_id[0])
+        return 0;
+    if ((av_gettime_relative() - rt->last_cmd_time) / 1000000 < rt->timeout / 2 &&
+        !rt->auth_state.stale)
+        return 0;
+    if (rt->server_type == RTSP_SERVER_WMS ||
+        (rt->server_type != RTSP_SERVER_REAL && rt->get_parameter_supported))
+        method = "GET_PARAMETER";
+    else
+        method = "OPTIONS";
+    ret = ff_rtsp_send_cmd(s, method, rt->control_uri, NULL, reply, NULL);
+    rt->auth_state.stale = 0;
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
+    if (reply->status_code != RTSP_STATUS_OK)
+        return ff_rtsp_averror(reply->status_code, -1);
+    return 0;
+}
+
 /* pause the stream */
 static int rtsp_read_pause(AVFormatContext *s)
 {
@@ -619,6 +650,8 @@ static int rtsp_read_set_state(AVFormatContext *s,
         case FF_INFMT_STATE_PLAY:
             return rtsp_read_play(s);
         case FF_INFMT_STATE_PAUSE:
+            if (((RTSPState *)s->priv_data)->state != RTSP_STATE_STREAMING)
+                return rtsp_keep_session_alive(s);
             return rtsp_read_pause(s);
         default:
             return AVERROR(ENOTSUP);
